72322"} "Don Quarrie"] ", the 1971 Pan American champion. The 1971 European Champion was " [:a {:href "/athletes/77390"} "Valery Borzov"] ", who had already won the 100 and was expected to challenge. Quarrie sustained a hamstring pull in the semis and did not qualify. Borzov dominated the final, winning by almost two metres over Black, with Italy’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/72052"} "Pietro Mennea"] " in third. Black was unfortunate to have drawn lane one in the final, but Borzov won the race by 0.19, so the result might not have changed even with a better lane draw. Borzov later became an IOC Member from Ukraine in 1994. He also married Soviet gymnastic legend " [:a {:href "/athletes/29216"} "Lyudmila Turishcheva"] ". His 100/200 double was the first ever won by a sprinter from outside North America. Fourth-place finisher " [:a {:href "/athletes/78181"} "Larry Burton"] " later played for five years in the NFL as a wide receiver for the New Orleans Saints and San Diego Chargers."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "QF"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "932"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/77390"} "Valery Borzov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "20.64 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "20.30w (1 h1)"] [:td {} "20.74 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "20.00 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "973"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78117"} "Larry Black"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "20.79 (1 h5)"]